================================================================================
Attribution and provenance
================================================================================

This project builds on the work of others, as CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 requires
it to acknowledge.

Quotation dataset
-----------------
The quotation dataset is derived from and adapted from the
"literature-clock" project by Johannes Enevoldsen (JohannesNE):

    https://github.com/JohannesNE/literature-clock

That collection is licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 2.5 Generic. Section 4(b)
of that license permits distributing an adaptation under a later version
of the same license, which is why this dataset is offered under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The non-commercial condition is inherited from it and
is not a restriction this project added.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/

That project in turn credits the e-reader literary clock by Jaap
Meijers.

Changes were made: quotes have been added, removed, edited, and
re-annotated (including the sfw / nsfw content ratings). Those
modifications are the responsibility of this project, not of the
original author.

Concept
-------
The underlying idea — telling the time through quotations from
literature — originated with a 2011 project at The Guardian and has been
reimplemented many times since.

